  "label": "The man giving a thumbs-up is mapped as the person experiencing a bad day.",
  "description": "The visual entity 'man' (specifically his thumbs-up gesture and neutral/slightly smiling expression) is mapped onto the textual entity 'having a bad day?' as the subject of the joke. The thumbs-up gesture, typically associated with positivity, is juxtaposed with the text to create a sarcastic or mocking tone, implying that the person is 'thumbs-up' for having a bad day — a humorous inversion. This mapping is reinforced by the overall hateful humor context, where the visual material (the man) is used to represent the person described in the text who is supposedly having a bad day.",
